course: dictionary
lesson: 8221
title: A surprising truth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A revelation is a surprising fact that comes out, often a secret that was hidden. When you meet this word, look at the clues around it. In a story, the big twist where the truth is finally shown is a revelation.
explain: Capital letters are clues too. «Some people later linked it to the Book of Revelation.» The capital R tells you Revelation is the name of a book, not an ordinary word. Ask: does the sentence describe a secret or a book? Then test your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Revelation can also mean something surprisingly good. «The new player was a revelation» means the player was far better than anyone expected. Try swapping in "surprising truth" or "surprisingly good thing" and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A revelation is a surprising fact that is made known, often a secret.
fact: Revelation can also mean the act of making something known.
fact: Something surprisingly good can be a revelation: «the new player was a revelation».
fact: In Christian belief, God shows truth to people by revelation.
fact: The Book of Revelation, with a capital R, is the last book of the New Testament in the Bible, full of visions about the end of the world.
exercise: «The new player was a revelation.» What does revelation mean here? | A rule for the game | *Someone surprisingly good | A long, boring match
exercise: «Some people later linked it to the Book of Revelation.» Why does Revelation start with a capital letter? | *It is the name of a special book | It starts a new sentence | It is the most important word in the sentence
exercise: In a story, a secret is uncovered at the end. What is this moment called? | A lullaby | A recipe | *A revelation | A ruler
test: «The discovery was a revelation to everyone.» Which meaning fits best? | A small, quiet room | *A surprising truth that came out | A type of bread | A long wait
test: Christians say God shows truth to people by what? | Confusion | A recipe | *Revelation | An exercise
exam: «The secret letter was a revelation.» Which meaning fits best? | A cold drink | A heavy box | *A surprising truth that came out | A school trip
